{
  "slug": "sciqlab-supply-chain",
  "name": "Sciqlab Supply Chain",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Three AI agents for supply chain operations — demand exception analysis, supplier risk scoring, and a multi-agent orchestrator for S&OP reviews. This plugin gives supply chain teams AI-powered demand planning and supplier risk intelligence, directly inside Claude. It includes three skills that work independently or together:\nDemand Exception Analyzer — Upload a CSV of historical sales vs forecast data and get MAPE/WMAPE calculations, forecast bias detection, consecutive exception flagging, and a VP-ready executive summary in seconds.\nSupplier Risk Assessment — Provide a list of suppliers and the agent researches each one via web search, then scores them across 6 risk dimensions (Financial Health, Geopolitical Risk, ESG, Supply Continuity, Compliance, Reputation) and generates a color-coded Excel report.\nMulti-Agent Orchestrator — Combines both agents into a single workflow: runs demand analysis first, identifies problem SKUs, then scores suppliers for those SKUs, and produces an integrated S&OP report with a P1-P4 priority action plan.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `demand-exception-analyzer` (Use this skill whenever a demand planning analyst needs to analyze historical sales vs forecast data, calculate forecast…), `inventory-analyst-skill` (Use this skill whenever an inventory analyst or supply chain planner needs to classify SKUs by ABC-XYZ methodology,…), `multi-agent-orchestrator` (Use this skill when a supply chain query requires demand planning analysis, supplier risk assessment, AND/OR inventory optimization…), `supplier-risk-assessment` (Run a two-step supplier risk assessment: (1) research suppliers from a CSV using Tavily web search, (2) score…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sciqlab-supply-chain@claude-community` from `tauseef-cmyk/Supply-Chain-Multi-Orchestrator-AI-Agent-Plug-ins` (`plugins/sciqlab-supply-chain`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
